.alert.alert-light.border
  %h3.fw-semibold.mb-2 Goal of this page
  %p.mb-3 Give managers a quick view of who is actively giving and receiving OGO feedback—and whether authored OGOs show a healthy mix of kudos and constructive ratings.

  %h3.fw-semibold.mb-2 Context
  %p.mb-3
    OGO Given and Received are Gruuv Health categories (Healthy / Warning / Needs Attention), same rules as 1:1 Hub Overview.
    Kudos mix and Rating intensity are separate culture signals from OGOs this person authored—not part of the row spotlight.

  %h3.fw-semibold.mb-2 Specifics of this page
  %h5.fw-semibold.mb-2 How to read each row
  %p.mb-3
    Given and Received drive the row spotlight (worst of the two). Use refresh controls only when you believe Gruuv Health or mix data is out of date and want to queue a background rebuild.

  %h5.fw-semibold.mb-2 Example employee row
  .card.mb-3
    .card-header.py-2
      %strong Example
    .card-body.py-2
      .table-responsive
        %table.table.table-sm.mb-2
          %thead
            %tr
              %th Employee
              %th Given
              %th Received
              %th Kudos mix
              %th Rating intensity
          %tbody
            %tr
              %td
                Alex Rivera
                %br
                %small.text-muted Casey Manager
              %td
                .alert.alert-success.mb-0.py-1.small
                  %strong Healthy
                  %div.text-muted 4 Healthy OGOs
              %td
                .alert.alert-warning.mb-0.py-1.small
                  %strong Warning
                  %div.text-muted 3 OGOs, 1 Warning
              %td
                .alert.alert-success.mb-0.py-1.small
                  %strong 4:1
                  %span.ms-1 Kudos: 4 | Constructive: 1
              %td
                .alert.alert-success.mb-0.py-1.small
                  %strong 3:1
                  %span.ms-1 Less extreme: 6 | Most extreme: 2
      .row.g-2.small
        .col-12.col-lg-6
          %div
            %i.bi.bi-arrow-up-right.me-1
            Hover Kudos mix and Rating intensity for why the ratio matters for that person.
          %div
            %i.bi.bi-arrow-up-right.me-1
            Hover Given or Received for Gruuv Health rules (#{EngagementHealth::Thresholds::OGO_HEALTHY_WITHIN_DAYS}/#{EngagementHealth::Thresholds::OGO_NEEDS_ATTENTION_AT_DAYS}-day windows).
            Healthy/Warning captions show band counts ("4 Healthy OGOs" or "3 OGOs, 1 Healthy"); Needs Attention shows count only (or Never published).
        .col-12.col-lg-6
          %div
            %i.bi.bi-arrow-up-right.me-1
            Spotlight counts use only Given + Received—not the mix columns.
          %div
            %i.bi.bi-arrow-up-right.me-1
            Refresh queues Gruuv Health + mix rebuild; data also refreshes on publish/unpublish and nightly.

  %h5.fw-semibold.mb-2 Status legend
  .row.mb-0
    .col-12.col-lg-6
      %p.fw-semibold.mb-2 Given & Received (Gruuv Health)
      %ul.mb-3.mb-lg-0
        %li
          %span.d-inline-block.rounded-circle.me-2.align-middle.bg-success{style: "width: 10px; height: 10px;"}
          %strong Healthy
          = " — published a qualifying OGO in the last #{EngagementHealth::Thresholds::OGO_HEALTHY_WITHIN_DAYS} days."
        %li
          %span.d-inline-block.rounded-circle.me-2.align-middle.bg-warning{style: "width: 10px; height: 10px;"}
          %strong Warning
          = " — last publish was #{EngagementHealth::Thresholds::OGO_HEALTHY_WITHIN_DAYS + 1}–#{EngagementHealth::Thresholds::OGO_NEEDS_ATTENTION_AT_DAYS - 1} days ago."
        %li
          %span.d-inline-block.rounded-circle.me-2.align-middle.bg-danger{style: "width: 10px; height: 10px;"}
          %strong Needs Attention
          = " — last publish was ≥ #{EngagementHealth::Thresholds::OGO_NEEDS_ATTENTION_AT_DAYS} days ago, or never."
    .col-12.col-lg-6
      %p.fw-semibold.mb-2 Kudos mix & Rating intensity
      %ul.mb-0
        %li
          %strong Kudos mix
          = " — kudos-style vs constructive OGOs authored (target about #{Insights::ObservationsRatingHealth::KUDOS_CONSTRUCTIVE_HEALTHY_RATIO_LABEL})."
        %li
          %strong Rating intensity
          = " — everyday (#{ObservationRating.display_label('agree')} + #{ObservationRating.display_label('disagree')}) vs extreme (#{ObservationRating.display_label('strongly_agree')} + #{ObservationRating.display_label('strongly_disagree')}) ratings on authored OGOs (target about 3:1)."
